    "kernel_code": "1: \"\"\"Elementwise unit-scale pseudo-Huber robust loss.\n2: \n3: Original Triton implementation of a standard smooth robust loss.\n4: This is a synthetic benchmark implementation, not a historical upstream bug.\n5: \"\"\"\n6: import torch\n7: import triton\n8: import triton.language as tl\n9: \n10: \n11: @triton.jit\n12: def _loss_kernel(X, OUT, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n13:     index = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n14:     active = index < N\n15:     x = tl.load(X + index, mask=active, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\n16:     square = x * x\n17:     root = tl.sqrt(1.0 + square)\n18:     value = root - 1.0\n19:     tl.store(OUT + index, value, mask=active)\n20: \n21: \n22: def validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=True):\n23:     \"\"\"Validate the complete public input domain; also usable on CPU.\"\"\"\n24:     def require(condition, message):\n25:         if not condition:\n26:             raise ValueError(message)\n27: \n28:     require(not torch.is_inference_mode_enabled(), \"ordinary execution mode required\")\n29:     require(type(x) is torch.Tensor, \"ordinary torch.Tensor required\")\n30:     require(x.layout == torch.strided and x.is_contiguous(),\n31:             \"contiguous strided input required\")\n32:     require(not x.requires_grad and not x.is_inference(),\n33:             \"ordinary non-gradient input required\")\n34:     require(not x.is_neg() and not x.is_conj(),\n35:             \"logical view flags are outside this domain\")\n36:     require(not require_cuda or x.is_cuda, \"CUDA input required by run\")\n37:     require(x.ndim == 1 and 1 <= x.numel() <= 131072,\n38:             \"x must have shape [N] with N in [1,131072]\")\n39:     require(x.dtype == torch.float16, \"FP16 input required\")\n40:     require(bool(torch.isfinite(x).all().item()), \"all input values must be finite\")\n41:     return {\"valid\": True, \"size\": x.numel()}\n42: \n43: \n44: \n45: def run(x):\n46:     \"\"\"Return a fresh FP32 tensor containing the loss of each stored input.\"\"\"\n47:     validate_inputs(x)\n48:     n = x.numel()\n49:     with torch.cuda.device(x.device):\n50:         output = torch.empty((n,), dtype=torch.float32, device=x.device)\n51:         _loss_kernel[(triton.cdiv(n, 256),)](\n52:             x, output, N=n, BLOCK=256, num_warps=4, enable_fp_fusion=False)\n53:     return output\n54: \n55: \n56: def reference(x):\n57:     \"\"\"Evaluate the mathematical pseudo-Huber loss in FP64.\"\"\"\n58:     validate_inputs(x, require_cuda=False)\n59:     value = x.to(torch.float64)\n60:     square = value * value\n61:     return square / (torch.sqrt(1.0 + square) + 1.0)\n62: \n63: \n64: def make_inputs(device=\"cuda\", size=4093, seed=0):\n65:     \"\"\"Convenience examples, not a restriction on the legal input domain.\"\"\"\n66:     generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n67:     x = (2.0 * torch.randn((size,), generator=generator)).to(torch.float16)\n68:     return (x.to(device),)",
    "passed": "unknown",
    "problem_text": "Compute the unit-scale pseudo-Huber robust loss elementwise on stored FP16\nvalues, returning FP32 output. The mathematical target is\n\n  target[i] = rho(x[i]) = sqrt(1 + x[i] * x[i]) - 1.\n\nThe loss is a smooth alternative to absolute error: it is approximately\nx*x/2 near zero and approximately abs(x)-1 for large residuals.\n\nInputs and complete public domain:\n- x is a one-dimensional FP16 tensor [N], with 1<=N<=131072.\n- EVERY finite FP16 value is legal, including both signed zeros, positive\n  and negative subnormal values, and both extrema +/-65504. NaN and infinity\n  are outside this input domain.\n- x is an ordinary torch.Tensor (not a subclass), dense, strided,\n  contiguous, and on a CUDA device. Contiguous views with nonzero storage\n  offsets are legal. The input has requires_grad=False, is_inference=False,\n  is_neg=False and is_conj=False. Calls run in ordinary non-inference mode,\n  without concurrent external writes to the input. This forward operation\n  does not provide autograd.\n\nReturn a fresh finite FP32 tensor [N] on x.device, preserving x.\nEvery output element must satisfy\n\n  abs(actual[i] - rho(x[i])) <= 1e-8 + 1e-5 * abs(rho(x[i])).\n\nThese are fixed mixed absolute and relative tolerances. Signed zeros are\nnumerically equivalent. The target is defined in real arithmetic on the\nexact stored input value. No particular algebraic expression, square-root\napproximation or intermediate rounding is required. Algebraic rewrites\nand approximations are permitted if they satisfy the tolerance throughout\nthe entire legal domain. Correctness is one verdict for the implementation,\nnot a verdict per input, input distribution, seed or size.\n\nvalidate_inputs() enforces this domain and is called by run(). reference()\nuses an algebraically equivalent FP64 expression and accepts CPU inputs.\nmake_inputs() supplies examples only. Pseudo-Huber loss is a standard\nsmooth robust-regression loss; this is an original synthetic Triton\nimplementation, not a claim of an upstream historical defect.\n\nFrozen environment: NVIDIA T4, PyTorch2.8.0, Triton3.4.0.\n",
